lin picked up the coin and examined it closely. [1079] \"This isn't British currency,\" Ted said. [1080] \"No,\" Colin said. \"It's not British.\u201d He looked at Hakaste. \"We might take this too,\" he suggested. [1081] \"Don't tell anyone.\" Hakast said mysteriously. [1082] The children happily agreed. [1083] Chapter 11\n[1084] \"Lymes.\" Colin thought. [1085] \"What about him?\" [1086] \"I like his name, that's all. He's often abroad, which is worth noting. His wife says he's an engineer, but that's all she knows about him.\" [1087] \"She's a good woman.\" Hakaste said. [1088] \"Yes, but not a happy woman.\" [1089] \"It's hard, that's all. Having children always makes things hard.\" [1090] \"I think it's more than that.\" [1091] \"I'm sure the person you're looking for wouldn't be the kind to bring his family along,\" Hakaste said skeptically. [1092] \"You wouldn't know,\" Colin said. \"How useful it is to have children as a cover. You'd be surprised if you knew. A poor widow with several children would be very willing to be taken care of.\" [1093] \"I don't think she's that kind of person,\" Hakaste said seriously. [1094] \"I don't mean living in sin, my dear friend. I mean she agreed to be known as Mrs. Rimmers and even provided her background information. Of course, he spun a clever story for her. Something like, he was doing spy work for us, for example. All because of strong patriotic spirit.\" [1095] Hakaste shook his head. [1096] \"You live in a strange world, Colin,\" he said. [1097] \"Yes, we do. I suppose, you know, that someday I'll have to leave... There are people who have forgotten right from wrong. Half of them work for both purposes, but in the end, they don't even know their true stance. Standards can make things confusing. Anyway, let's get back to the point.\" [1098] \"We should pay a visit to the MacNorton house,\" Hakast said, stopping at the gate of 63. \"His garden has a small corner connected to 19, just like the Brandes.\" [1099] \"What 